{
  "_about": [
    "The languages a client in the five northern regions may need, and where each is spoken.",
    "Codes are ISO 639-3 (English stays 'en', as CHT uses it). A code of null means it has not been confirmed.",
    "District lists are a starting point from published sources. Each District Health Directorate confirms",
    "its own list before its district joins (docs/LANGUAGES.md). 'tier' is the order of work, not importance:",
    "1 = needed for the Kumbungu pilot; 2 = a region's main language, needed before that region joins;",
    "3 = served through a CHW or interpreter until a speaker community and reviewers are found.",
    "'bgl' = has a Bureau of Ghana Languages standard orthography (11 older languages; Kusaal, Likpakpaanl and",
    "Sisaali added in 2026). 'resources' lists what is publicly LISTED by the provider; nothing is verified",
    "for health use until we have tested it with speakers."
  ],
  "languages": {
    "en": { "name": "English", "tier": 1, "regions": ["northern", "savannah", "north_east", "upper_east", "upper_west"], "role": "Official language; the nurses' working language and the source text for every translation." },

